# File Organization

## File Naming (all kebab-case)

| Type | Pattern | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| Component | `<name>.vue` | `runai-btn.vue` |
| Store | `<name>.store.ts` | `app.store.ts` |
| Service | `<name>.service.ts` | `user.service.ts` |
| Composable | `use-<name>.composable.ts` | `use-refresh.composable.ts` |
| Model | `<name>.model.ts` | `config.model.ts` |
| Utility | `<name>.util.ts` | `date.util.ts` |
| Test | `<name>.test.ts` | `cluster.store.test.ts` |

## Import Order

Group imports with comments: vue → stores → components → models → services → utils → constants → routes

See `src/App.vue` for canonical import organization.

## Key Patterns

- Always use `@/` alias for src imports
- Tests are co-located with source files
- Components use `index.ts` for exports: See `src/components/common/runai-btn/index.ts`
- Utils export as object: See `src/utils/date.util/date.util.ts`

## Do NOT Edit

- `src/swagger-models/` - Auto-generated from API specs
